\par Mrs Chain appeared in the doorway, saw the mugs, and muttered something so compressed and eloquent that Neville felt it should possibly be preserved for future constitutional use.
\par He opened the tea caddy.
\par Inside were sachets.
\par \'93Dear God,\'94 he said.
\par Beatrix leaned in. \'93What.\'94
\par \'93Bagged herbal alternatives.\'94
\par Mrs Chain gripped the counter. \'93No.\'94
\par Jago peered over Neville\rquote s shoulder. \'93Lemon serenity.\'94
\par Mrs Chain shut her eyes. \'93Mr Wren, if at any point it becomes necessary to break the law in order to restore my kitchen, I should like you to know in advance that I am philosophically available.\'94
\par Neville was about to reply when the wall clock in the sitting room chimed eleven.
\par A moment later, the kitchen clock chimed ten forty-eight.
\par Then, somewhere upstairs, another clock struck noon with irritating confidence.
\par All four of them froze.
\par Beatrix said, \'93That\rquote s not acceptable.\'94
\par \'93No,\'94 said Neville.
\par \'93Why not,\'94 said Jago, \'93from a strictly theoretical standpoint.\'94
\par \'93Because,\'94 said Neville, \'93the house is failing to collapse consistently.\'94
\par There was a brief silence.
\par Then Beatrix looked at him. \'93Explain.\'94
\par Neville set the tea caddy down very carefully, as one does with explosive materials and herbal substitutes.
\par \'93If the Ministry is simplifying places into single stable versions,\'94 he said, \'93then this house should at least settle on one. But it hasn\rquote t. It\rquote 
s been forced into a revised state too early, before the underlying details agreed with one another.\'94
\par Mrs Chain folded her arms. \'93So it\rquote s not my proper house and not a proper replacement either.\'94
\par \'93Yes.\'94
\par \'93It\rquote s botched.\'94
\par \'93Yes.\'94
\par Jago nodded appreciatively. \'93That\rquote s almost comforting.\'94
\par Neville took out the green notebook and wrote:
\par Premature collapse }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af2\afs20 \ltrch\fcs0 \f2\fs20\kerning0\insrsid2375315\charrsid2375315 \\neq}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \f0\kerning0\insrsid2375315\charrsid2375315  stable reality
\par Then below it:
\par Forcing one answer too early leaves incompatible details trapped inside the result.
\par Beatrix was already moving again, opening cupboards, checking drawers, pulling at labels with the brisk resolve of an auditor committed to making the world justify itself.
\par \'93In here,\'94 she said.
\par They joined her in a small room at the back of the hall which Mrs Chain identified, with indignation, as the airing cupboard.
\par A white sticker had been fixed above the handle.
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\f0\kerning0\insrsid2375315\charrsid2375315 OPTIONAL LINEN SPACE}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \f0\kerning0\insrsid2375315\charrsid2375315 
\par Mrs Chain stared at it as if she had finally found the exact point at which civilization had given up.
\par \'93It is not optional,\'94 she said.
\par Beatrix held up a folded sheet of paper she had found wedged behind the towels.
\par \'93It gets worse.\'94
\par The sheet was a checklist.
