\par No one spoke.
\par Even Jago, who seemed to consider silence a hobby for other people, looked briefly without charm.
\par Mrs Chain took the paper from Beatrix.
\par \'93Identity trimming,\'94 she said.
\par Neville nodded once.
\par She looked at him with a terrible steadiness. \'93That means me.\'94
\par \'93Yes.\'94
\par The house, perhaps sensing that it had been discussed too accurately, made a small sound overhead. Not a creak. More a correction.
\par Then, from the sitting room, came the flat electronic ding of an arriving message.
\par They returned to find the rectangular mirror in the hall faintly lit.
\par Words were appearing across its surface in blue.
