This chapter teaches two linked ideas: the }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\f0\kerning0\insrsid14165747\charrsid14165747 no-cloning theorem}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \f0\kerning0\insrsid14165747\charrsid14165747  and }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 
\ltrch\fcs0 \b\f0\kerning0\insrsid14165747\charrsid14165747 quantum error correction}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \f0\kerning0\insrsid14165747\charrsid14165747 .
\par The no-cloning theorem states that there is no physical process that can make an exact, independent copy of an arbitrary unknown quantum state. This is not an engineering limitation to be overcome with better funding \emdash 
 it follows directly from the lineari
ty of quantum evolution. If cloning were possible, you could copy a state, measure the copy destructively, and learn the original without disturbing it, which would break the measurement structure of quantum mechanics entirely (and, incidentally, permit f
aster-than-light signalling). This is why Voller's vault is a fraud he did not know he was committing: he recorded measurement outcomes, which are classical, and believed he had recorded a state, which is not.
\par The complementarity underneath it is the same principle that drove Chapter Four. Measuring in one basis destroys the information encoded in the conjugate one. The Ministry asked "which wallpaper?" and got an answer; the price of that answer was the phase 
relations that made the house a coherent whole rather than a list of features.
\par Quantum error correction is the escape route, and it is genuinely counterintuitive. Since you cannot copy a state, you instead }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\f0\kerning0\insrsid14165747\charrsid14165747 encode}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 
\f0\kerning0\insrsid14165747\charrsid14165747  it redundantly across many physical systems, so that no small subset of them carries the full information \emdash  and therefore no local damage can destroy it. Recovery works by measuring }{\rtlch\fcs1 
\ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\f0\kerning0\insrsid14165747\charrsid14165747 syndromes}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \f0\kerning0\insrsid14165747\charrsid14165747 
: cleverly chosen joint observables that reveal what error occurred without revealing anything about the encoded state itself. That is Fainrose's line about asking whether the left hand and right hand still agree. You learn the injury without collapsing t
he patient.
\par And the ordering matters. Correction operations need not commute, which is why Chapter Seven's warning \emdash  LOCAL RECOVERY NO LONGER COMMUTATIVE \emdash  is now the operational problem rather than an alarming noun.
\par }\pard \ltrpar\ql \li0\ri0\sb100\sa100\sbauto1\saauto1\widctlpar\wrapdefault\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\outlinelevel2\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid14165747 {\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0\afs27 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\f0\fs27\kerning0\insrsid14165747\charrsid14165747 
