 grey tie, and gloves. He held a hat. He gave the impression of a person who had been standing there for some time, waiting to be noticed, and who considered impatience a form of bad manners.
\par "I am sorry to intrude," he said. His English was slow, and exact, and unhurried in a way that made Neville realise how fast everybody else had been speaking for three days. "May I present myself. Louis-Raymond-Victor, Duc de Br\'e9vanne."
\par Neville got up. He was not entirely sure why, except that one did.
\par "Neville Wren."
\par "Yes. Transit Reconciliation." De Br\'e9vanne inclined his head very slightly. "I have read your notebook."
\par "You have not."
