aurice's papers from the 1911 Solvay congress, and really did make his central proposal in a 1924 doctoral thesis. The move was almost embarrassingly simple: Einstein had shown that light, long known as a wave, carries momentum in discrete quanta. De Brog
lie asked the mirror question \emdash  if waves have particle character, do particles have wave character? \emdash  and wrote down the relation
