for any locally realistic theory, while quantum mechanics predicts values up to }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af2\afs20 \ltrch\fcs0 \f2\fs20\kerning0\insrsid2584713\charrsid2584713 2\\sqrt\{2\} \\approx 2.83}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 
\f0\kerning0\insrsid2584713\charrsid2584713 . The bound is derived from school-level algebra plus the two assumptions, which is the source of its authority: it is not an interpretation but a constraint that any locally real world must satisfy.
\par Experiment has settled it. Freedman and Clauser (1972), Aspect (1981\endash 82), and then a generation of loophole-closing work \emdash 
 Weihs and Zeilinger on locality, Delft on detection efficiency and event-ready entanglement, the Big Bell Test on freedom-of-choice \emdash  all report violation, and the 2022 Nobel Prize in Physics went to Clauser, Aspect, and Zeilinger for it. }{
\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\f0\kerning0\insrsid2584713\charrsid2584713 Nature is not locally real.}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \f0\kerning0\insrsid2584713\charrsid2584713  
At least one of the two comfortable assumptions must go, and every interpretation on the market pays that price somewhere: pilot-wave theory (Chapter Twelve) keeps realism and abandons locality outright; many worlds keeps locality by abandoning single-out
come definiteness; operationalism declines to have the conversation.
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\f0\kerning0\insrsid2584713\charrsid2584713 Why this is the plot's weapon.}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \f0\kerning0\insrsid2584713\charrsid2584713  
Bell's result is interpretation-neutral and experimentally established, which makes it the one thing in the novel that cannot be dismissed as metaphysics before a committee. And it bears directly on the Ministry's legal architecture: the Board's defence r
ests on nine thousand dwellings having been surveyed as independent local systems, each certificate separately defensible. A measured Bell violation across the correlation lattice would establish, without reference to any interpretation, that they were ne
ver independent \emdash  collapsing nine thousand small administrative matters into one indivisible act.
