\par "Yes," said Leonhard von Wittenberg. "And so the current view \emdash  not proven, not settled, but the view \emdash 
 is that evaporation does not destroy the information. It is scrambled almost beyond recovery, it emerges in correlations so subtle that no practical me
asurement could unpick them, but it is not annihilated. Unitarity survives. The books balance." He put the sheet down. "Tell Halpert that the ledger is not kept in the vault. It is kept on the wall."
