\par At half past six Neville walked back to the school hall through streets that were still visibly deciding things, and found Fainrose sitting on a crate eating a sandwich beside a rack of timing electronics.
\par "You've been with von Wittenberg," she said. "You've got the expression. Everyone gets the expression."
\par "He says everything is eleven-dimensional membranes."
\par "Yes."
\par "And that the record of everything the Ministry dumped into 4C is written on the horizon rather than inside it, so it can't be destroyed by evaporation."
\par Fainrose stopped chewing.
