: the physics of a region can be fully encoded on its boundary, one dimension lower. Its precise realisation is the AdS/CFT correspondence, in which a gravitational theory in anti-de Sitter space is exactly dual to a conformal field theory on its boundary
. Applied to the information paradox of Chapter Six, this supports the now-mainstream expectation that evaporation is unitary \emdash 
 the information is not destroyed inside and annihilated, but encoded at the horizon and released in the radiation's fine correlations, scrambled to the point of practical unrecoverability but preserved in principle.
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\f0\kerning0\insrsid2584713\charrsid2584713 The honest caveat.}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \f0\kerning0\insrsid2584713\charrsid2584713 
 None of this is experimentally confirmed. String theory has produced no testable prediction at accessible energies, and critics \emdash  Fainrose's position, and Bellew's \emdash 
 hold that a framework this flexible risks being unfalsifiable. The chapter does not resolve that, and should not.
